course: dictionary
lesson: 8203
title: One word, two very different meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Retard» is a good example. As a formal word (said ri-TARD), it means to slow down or delay something. Scientists use it for slowing growth or a reaction, and fire-retardant material slows burning.
explain: The other meaning is a hurtful insult, used to be cruel to people, especially people with a learning disability. It is never a kind word, and you must never use it, even as a joke. When you read it in a story, notice that it shows a character being unkind, and ask how the person it is aimed at might feel.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. «On est en retard !» is French, and it means "we're late!" In French, retard means late, so the shouting friend is hurrying for the bus. Always check the clues around the word, then check your meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Old medical words used to describe learning difficulties have been replaced by kinder words, such as «learning disability». Choosing respectful words shows that you care about everyone's feelings.
fact: Retard (said ri-TARD) is a formal verb meaning to slow down or delay something.
fact: Fire-retardant material slows burning, which helps keep people safe.
fact: In French, retard means late, as in «On est en retard !» ("we're late!").
fact: The insult sense of retard is very hurtful: never use it, even as a joke.
fact: Use kinder words, such as learning disability, instead of old medical or insulting words.
exercise: In a science lesson, what does retard mean? | Shine brightly | Make something faster | *To slow down or delay something | Hurt someone's feelings
exercise: Fire-retardant material is used to do what? | *Slow down burning to keep people safe | Keep things cold | Stop the rain | Make things burn brighter
exercise: In «On est en retard !», what does retard mean? | Fast | *Late | Early | Lost
test: Why should you never use the insult sense of retard? | It is a formal science word | It means slow down | *It hurts people, especially people with learning disabilities
test: Which kinder phrase replaces old medical words for learning difficulties? | Slowcoach | *Learning disability | Fire-retardant | Late
exam: What should you do when you hear retard used as a hurtful insult? | Learn to say it louder | Repeat it as a joke | Use it to tease a friend | *Remember it hurts people, and never repeat it
